
  Stop every job the run daemon runs in each worktree named, or in the one you stand in.
  With --profile, only that profile's jobs stop; with --all, every worktree of this repository's,
  never another repository's. Several worktrees stop at once.

  A shared service a worktree holds is released: it runs on for the worktrees still holding it, and
  stops with its last hold. A stack stops by its stop command. A job that crashed is cleared.
  A worktree removed while its jobs ran is named by its path.

  Usage:
    wtm-next run down [worktree...] [flags]

  Examples:
    # The jobs of the worktree you stand in
    wtm run down

    # Two worktrees, one profile's jobs only
    wtm run down feat/login fix/typo --profile backend

    # Every worktree of this repository, for a script or an agent
    wtm run down --all --yes --output json

  Flags:
        --all                         Stop the jobs of every worktree of this repository
        --ask                         Ask again the questions this repository remembers an answer to, to change or forget it
    -n, --dry-run                     Show the plan and its fingerprint, apply nothing
        --expect-fingerprint string   Apply only if the facts still have this fingerprint, the one --dry-run printed
    -h, --help                        help for down
        --output string               Output format: text or json (default "text")
        --profile string              Stop only this profile's jobs (default: every job the worktree runs)
    -y, --yes                         Run unattended: no question, no confirmation (the worktree you stand in unless given)

  Global Flags:
    -q, --quiet   Silence human output; errors and the exit code are unaffected, and --output json still emits its document

